    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic is making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a worn one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a long, ribbed belt that powers various accessories in your engine, like the alternator, power steering pump, and AC compressor. When this belt wears down, it can lose its necessary tension or develop cracks, which causes it to slip on the pulleys. This slipping action, especially under the increased load of accelerating, is what generates that loud squealing sound. If needed, replacing the belt is usually a relatively straightforward and affordable fix.",
      "source": "target",
