    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the info. i tried looking at it and i dont see anything obvious like cracks or dirt. it's just this weird intermittent squeal. sometimes it feels like there's just something random messing with it, like a glitch or something. is there any way to tell if it's a part failing or just some weird electrical or mechanical interference?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An intermittent squeal that doesn't show visible signs of wear often suggests an issue with tensioning or a small, developing failure within a pulley bearing. A purely electrical interference is highly unlikely to cause a mechanical squealing sound related to engine accessories. If the noise is truly random, the tensioner pulley itself might be worn out, allowing the belt to fluctuate in tension unexpectedly. Having a mechanic lift the car and monitor the belt while you accelerate is the best way to diagnose this elusive \"glitch.\"",
      "source": "target",
